# Vesti TypeScript Architecture
- Use TypeScript throughout.
- Prefer explicit typed props and predictable state flow.
- Reuse existing functions and handlers before introducing duplicate logic.
- Keep new components focused and feature-oriented.
- Do not perform broad refactors during visual design tasks.
- Avoid adding abstractions that do not solve a current problem.
- Protect existing AI generation, product catalog, analytics, commerce, and Cloudflare logic.
- Treat src/App.tsx as high-risk legacy code: make minimal targeted changes.
- When adding state, check for stale-state and cross-flow contamination.
- Before changing a working flow, trace the current state transitions first.
- Remove dead code only when the task specifically includes cleanup and regression checks.
